WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
The New Forest, in southern England.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:07.470
Ancient woodland, open heath, and
ponies grazing the open forest.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.470
Every year it gets over
15 million day-visits,

4
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.370
for walking, cycling and riding.

5
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.190
Its timber once went into ship-building.

6
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.490
Woodlands like these are
habitats for rare wildlife.

7
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.710
So can a forest this busy be
both enjoyed and protected?

8
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.630
In this mission, you'll sort
what a woodland gives us,

9
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.210
and find out why so much
woodland has been lost.

10
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.650
Then you'll meet the people
who manage the New Forest,

11
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.590
and judge whether their approach works.

12
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.450
Your mission: decide whether the New
Forest's visitors and its wildlife can both

13
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.170
win.
